## ServiceLoader provider constructors modeled

For every interface actually resolved above, the registered providers for it
(SERVICE_LOADING S2) — each one's public no-argument constructor is added as a
call-graph target from the resolving call site, plus a related edge to the provider's
own class-initializer if it has one. A registration whose interface nothing resolved
to calls for is correctly left out (not a gap — nothing asks for it). "Gap" explains
why a found, used provider still got no constructor target (e.g. no public
no-argument constructor) — a missing implementation, not evidence the provider is
unreachable. This still only covers the constructor itself: no iterator/`Provider.get`
method call on the resulting instance is modeled (SERVICE_LOADING S2's own remaining
scope).
