## Callback registration call sites

Every call site found matching, or nearly matching, a cataloged callback-registration
API (`java.lang.Thread`'s Runnable-taking constructors, `Executor`/`ExecutorService`'s
`execute`/`submit`; ASYNC_CALLBACKS A0). **Not a call-graph edge** — this says a method
*registers* a callback with an API that will eventually invoke it, not what the
callback actually is or that it ever runs (resolving the callback argument's concrete
type is ASYNC_CALLBACKS A1; turning that into a call-graph edge is A2, neither
implemented yet). "unsupported-api" means the call's owner and method name match a
cataloged API and the call plausibly still passes a callback argument, but this exact
overload isn't cataloged — a real registration ariadne doesn't model yet, not a false
negative being hidden.
